    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d775">

                <pb facs="0860" n="848" xml:id="pg848"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48 Refugees/2305a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in the
                        United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-11-16T19:00:00-05:00">November 16,
                            1940—7 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3510. You may, at the request to us of interested Jewish groups in the United
                    States, make a <hi rendition="#italic">pro forma</hi> inquiry of the Foreign
                    Office as to the veracity of reports which have been received by Jewish circles
                    from Syria to the effect that the British authorities in Palestine will not
                    permit 1700 refugees of German and Austrian origin to land from a Greek ship now
                    off the Palestine coast and are suggesting that they proceed to Mauritius.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
